> t1(x: u8) = x + 1
> t2(x: u8) = x + 2
> equiv t1 t2
t1 and t2 differ at 256 points, e.g. x=0: 1 vs 2
> u1(x: u8) = (x + 1) - 1
> u2(x: u8) = x
> equiv u1 u2
u1 and u2 are equal on the domain of u1 (exhaustive)
> s1(x: i8) = -x
> s2(x: i8) = 0 - x
> equiv s1 s2
s1 and s2 are equal on the domain of s1 (exhaustive)
> s3(x: i8) = x * 3
> s4(x: i8) = 3 * x
> equiv s3 s4
s3 and s4 are equal on the domain of s3 (exhaustive)
> w1(x: u16) = (x << 3) - (x << 2)
> w2(x: u16) = x << 2
> equiv w1 w2
w1 and w2 are equal on the domain of w1 (exhaustive)
> w3(x: i16) = (x*2)/2
> w4(x: i16) = x
> equiv w3 w4
w3 and w4 differ at 32768 points, e.g. x=-32768: 0 vs -32768
> d1(x: u8) = 100 / (x + 1)
> d2(x: u8) = 100 / (1 + x)
> equiv d1 d2
d1 and d2 are equal on the domain of d1 (exhaustive)
> r1(x: real) = x*x
> r2(x: real) = x^2
> equiv r1 r2
r1 and r2 are equal on the domain of r1 (sampled, not proved; no SAT proof: a real value)
